  "term": "electrocardiogram",
  "definition": "An electrocardiogram, or ECG, is a non-invasive and relatively low-cost test that records heart-related electrical activity and is widely used to help identify cardiovascular disease. In learning contexts, ECG data are also used for computer-based classification and anomaly detection.",
